      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "steps_unavailable": "Pre-predicate adverb plus an obligatory negative predicate. The record's formation is なかなか + [verb in the 〜ない / 〜ません form], so なかなか stands BEFORE the predicate and applies no operation to it, and the closed op enum has no prepend operation. Steps covering only the negative half would emit 書かない as if it were the pattern, and the ない cannot be dropped either: the record states that なかなか with an affirmative predicate means something else entirely ('quite / surprisingly good').",
