    {
      "slug": "gram:nowa-da",
      "nuance_tags": ["emphasis"],
      "usage_contexts": ["spoken", "written"],
      "steps_unavailable": "Two-slot cleft frame, not a derivation from one base. The record's formation is [clause in plain form] + のは + [element in focus] + だ/です: the second slot is a free element (noun, place, time) supplied independently, so an ordered chain built from a single base cannot produce the pattern's surface. Steps covering only the left half would emit 行くのは / 好きなのは as if that were the pattern, the same defect flagged for the other multi-slot templates in this set. The left-half rule the record does state is: verbs and い-adjectives take the plain form directly before のは, な-adjectives take 〜な (好きなのは).",
